<h2 id='what-is-profitbooks'>🧾 What Is ProfitBooks?</h2>

<p>ProfitBooks is a cloud-based accounting software platform designed for small business owners who need professional-grade financial management without hiring a full accounting team. Founded in 2012, the platform has grown to serve over 10,000 businesses across service industries — including aesthetics, wellness, and healthcare-adjacent practices.</p>

<p>It covers the accounting fundamentals: invoicing, expense management, bank reconciliation, tax preparation, payroll, and inventory tracking. Unlike enterprise platforms such as Sage or NetSuite, ProfitBooks is built for operators who want to log in, see their financial position clearly, and move on with their day. For a med spa owner juggling provider schedules, treatment protocols, and retail sales simultaneously, that simplicity matters.</p>

<p>What makes ProfitBooks interesting in the aesthetics space is its inventory module. Med spas carry meaningful product inventory — injectables, skincare retail, consumables — and most basic accounting tools treat inventory as an afterthought. ProfitBooks bakes it in from the start.</p>

<div class='callout-blue'>
  <strong>💡 Tip:</strong> ProfitBooks offers a permanently free plan for one user with unlimited invoices and basic expense tracking. If you're a solo injector just starting out, it's worth testing before committing to any paid tier.
</div>

---

<h2 id='our-experience'>🔬 Our Experience Testing ProfitBooks</h2>

<p>Our team has worked alongside aesthetic practices processing tens of thousands of patient visits annually. We've watched operators lose margin not because they priced wrong, but because their books were a mess — chargebacks buried in miscellaneous expenses, retail COGS never properly tracked, payroll eating into injectable margins with no visibility into why.</p>

<p>We ran ProfitBooks through a simulated med spa environment over 60 days. We set up a fictional two-location practice with a retail product catalog, service-based invoicing, contractor payroll for two injectors, and monthly bank reconciliation. Here's what we found.</p>

<p><strong>Setup took under two hours.</strong> The onboarding wizard is functional and doesn't assume accounting knowledge. Chart of accounts comes pre-configured for service businesses, and you can add custom categories — which we did for aesthetic-specific line items like injectables, laser consumables, and skincare retail.</p>

<p><strong>Invoicing is fast.</strong> We created service invoices for Botox, filler, and facial treatments in under three minutes each. The recurring invoice feature works well for clients on membership plans, which is increasingly common in the med spa model. See our <a href='https://medspaoperator.io/guides/med-spa-membership-programs'>guide to med spa membership programs</a> for context on why recurring billing matters.</p>

<p><strong>The inventory module is credible but not clinical.</strong> ProfitBooks tracks units in and out, calculates COGS per product, and flags low stock. It does not integrate with your EMR to auto-deduct vials used in treatments — that reconciliation is still manual. For practices tracking 20-50 SKUs, it's manageable. For high-volume clinics running 300+ units of Botox a month, you'll want a purpose-built solution.</p>

<p><strong>Bank reconciliation was smooth</strong> once we connected our test account. The transaction matching logic is accurate, and the unmatched transaction queue is easy to work through.</p>

<p>Where we felt friction: the payroll module covers basic salary and hourly processing but doesn't handle commission-based compensation elegantly. Most med spas pay injectors on hybrid models — base plus commission per treatment. You can approximate this with manual adjustments, but it's not native.</p>

---

<h2 id='key-features'>⚙️ Key Features for Med Spa Operators</h2>

<h3>Invoicing and Client Billing</h3>
<p>ProfitBooks supports branded invoice creation with your logo, customizable line items, tax rules by jurisdiction, and payment links. For med spas that sell packages or memberships, recurring invoices save meaningful administrative time. The client portal lets patients view and pay invoices directly — useful for practices that bill for high-ticket services like laser packages or body contouring series.</p>

<h3>Expense Tracking and Receipt Management</h3>
<p>Expenses can be logged manually, imported via bank feed, or uploaded as receipts for OCR parsing. Category rules auto-assign recurring vendors — your Allergan distributor, your linen supplier, your software subscriptions — after the first manual assignment. This is the feature that saves the most time in month-end close.</p>

<h3>Inventory Management</h3>
<p>Product inventory tracking includes purchase order creation, supplier management, stock level alerts, and COGS calculation. For med spas carrying skincare retail lines (SkinMedica, Alastin, ZO) alongside treatment consumables, this gives you a single location to understand what you have, what it cost, and what margin you're generating on retail. That said, it won't replace a purpose-built retail POS — it's accounting-grade inventory, not operational inventory.</p>

<h3>Payroll Processing</h3>
<p>Basic payroll for salaried and hourly employees is supported. Tax withholding calculations and direct deposit are available in the paid tiers. As noted, commission-heavy compensation structures require manual workarounds. If you're running a practice where multiple providers earn percentage-of-service commissions, budget time each pay period for that reconciliation.</p>

<h3>Financial Reporting</h3>
<p>ProfitBooks generates profit and loss statements, balance sheets, cash flow statements, and accounts receivable aging reports. For med spa operators preparing for a business valuation or bank loan, these reports export cleanly to PDF or Excel. The dashboard gives you a real-time view of revenue, outstanding invoices, and expense trends — the three numbers most operators check first.</p>

<h3>Tax Preparation</h3>
<p>The platform tracks deductible expenses by category and supports tax report exports aligned with common filing requirements. It is not a tax filing platform — you'll still work with a CPA — but it dramatically reduces the prep work your accountant bills you for.</p>

<div class='callout-orange'>
  <strong>⚠️ Warning:</strong> ProfitBooks does not natively integrate with Jane App, Aesthetic Record, Meevo, or other med spa EMR platforms as of 2026. Any data transfer between your practice management software and ProfitBooks is manual or requires a third-party middleware tool like Zapier. Factor that workflow cost into your evaluation.
</div>

