<h2 id='final-verdict'>🏁 Final Verdict</h2>

<p>ProfitBooks earns a <strong>4.1 out of 5</strong> from our team for med spa operators in the solo-to-dual-location range. The pricing is genuinely competitive, the inventory module is a legitimate differentiator, and the interface removes the friction that causes most operators to avoid their books until tax season forces the issue.</p>

<p>The gaps are real — no EMR integration, limited commission payroll, constrained multi-location reporting — but they're gaps that many small med spa operators won't hit in day-to-day operations. If you're spending $60-90 a month on QuickBooks and using 30% of its features, ProfitBooks at $15-30 a month likely covers everything you actually need.</p>

<p>The 30-day free trial and permanent free plan mean there's no financial risk to testing it against your current setup. We'd recommend running it in parallel with your existing tool for one billing cycle before committing.</p>

